<title>UK: Abattoir report was not suppressed - UK's Major.</title>
<headline>Abattoir report was not suppressed - UK's Major.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major on Thursday denied claims that the government had deliberately suppressed a report showing unhealthy conditions in Britain's abattoirs.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no question of the report being suppressed. It was very widely circulated. It was circulated around the trade and elsewhere,&quot; Major told parliament at question time.</p>
<p>But Major said the report was not seen by ministers.</p>
<p>The report by the government's Meat Hygiene Service, leaked to the Financial Times newspaper, concluded that the abattoirs were potential breeding grounds for the E-coli organism that killed at least 20 people through food poisoning in Scotland.</p>
<p>Agriculture Minister Douglas Hogg is due to make a statement to parliament on the matter at 1530 gmt.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
